1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,580
Okay, Chandler.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,580
Okay.

3
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,670
And your horoscope says:

4
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:09,250
"On the 5th, a special someone is going to give you a gift."

5
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:12,050
Oh, well, thank you in advance. Mm.

6
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:12,050
Ha, ha.

7
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:14,760
"But the 12th brings a lover's spat."

8
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:17,550
You're going to make a joke about my special present.

9
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:20,850
Why would you do that?

10
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:25,730
Oh, wait. "On the 19th, a secret crush announces itself."

11
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,650
Hey, guys.

12
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,650
Hey.

13
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:35,200
Oh, my God! It's Joey Tribbiani of Mac and C.H.E.E.S.E.

14
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:40,120
That's right. It's your first day.

15
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,580
Are you psyched to fight fake crime with your robot sidekick?

16
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:46,250
Am I psyched? The lead in my own TV series?

17
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:48,830
I've dreamed about this for years.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,420
Why have I not been preparing?

19
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:54,760
No, Joey, you're gonna be great.

20
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:58,590
But I gotta act with a robot. I don't know anything about technology.

21
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,720
I can't even use Chandler's computer, except to find porn.

22
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:06,230
And that's only because it's there when you turn it on.

23
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,980
Our lover's spat will start a little early this month.

24
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:12,440
I'll be waiting.

25
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:58,070
Are you judging them by their covers? Because you're really not supposed to.

26
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:01,950
I'm deciding which one to use. I'm going to start writing another book.

27
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:05,870
Because the last one was such a big seller?

28
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:10,000
Well, if you must know, I have written 14 books.

29
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:12,540
And as I'm the only one who has read them...

30
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:16,260
I can tell you that they have all been very well received.

31
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:19,050
Hey.

32
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:19,050
Hey.

33
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:20,970
Hi.

34
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:20,970
What are you doing later?

35
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:23,470
Oh, Rachel and I have to get our hair cut.

36
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,640
We do?

37
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:26,640
I want to see what he wants first.

38
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:30,770
I just found out Elizabeth's dad wants to meet me.

39
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,560
Wait a minute. Hold the phone.

40
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:35,070
You're not Elizabeth's dad?

41
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,740
Come on, guys. I really want this guy to like me.

42
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:43,490
It would really help me out if you guys could be here...

43
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,830
to make me look good.

44
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,830
Of course we'll help.

45
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:47,540
We'll be here.

46
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:47,540
Thanks.

47
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,540
We know how tough those parent-teacher conferences can be.

48
00:02:55,880 --> 00:03:00,510
So here's your office set.

49
00:02:55,880 --> 00:03:00,510
Wow, huh?

50
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,970
Mac Machiavelli, Private Investigator. Eh?

51
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,680
Let's get you to wardrobe for a fitting.

52
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,680
Okay.

53
00:03:07,850 --> 00:03:09,640
Hey, uh, when do I meet the robot?

54
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:12,100
Why don't we do that right now? He's right here.

55
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:14,770
Okay.

56
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:14,770
Joey Tribbiani, this is...

57
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:18,190
Wow! He's so lifelike.

58
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:20,570
Unbelievable.

59
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:23,660
This is Wayne, the man who created and operates C.H.E.E.S.E.

60
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:26,030
How do you do there, buddy?

61
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:29,290
I'll let you two guys get acquainted, huh?

62
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:29,290
Okay.

63
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:30,790
Sorry about that.

64
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:35,880
Uh, so where's C.H.E.E.S.E?

65
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:35,880
C.H.E.E.S.E. is right here.

66
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:43,340
Nice to meet you, Mac.

67
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:50,350
This is the temporary robot, right?

68
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:50,350
No. Why?

69
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:53,810
Well, I just thought it was gonna be a really cool robot.

70
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:57,150
Like the Terminator, or, uh, when I first saw you.

71
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:01,940
I spent two years developing this machine. It's absolutely state of the art.

72
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:05,450
I'm sorry. It doesn't look like it can do anything.

73
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,660
It can do this.

74
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,830
Hey... Oh, ha, ha.

75
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:23,260
This is my father, Paul Stevens. Dad, this is Ross Geller.

76
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:25,840
It's great to meet you, Paul.

77
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:29,470
I prefer that Liz's boyfriends to address me as Mr. Stevens.

78
00:04:30,810 --> 00:04:33,020
Uh, of course. Mr. Stevens.

79
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,480
Good. So, Ross...

80
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:37,900
what's your problem?

81
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,110
Excuse me?

82
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,280
Why can't you get a girlfriend your own age?

83
00:04:43,990 --> 00:04:46,200
Heh. It's funny...

84
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:49,530
Um, it's not funny.

85
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,370
I don't like you going out with my daughter, Ross.

86
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:55,290
Okay, um, I can see that.

87
00:04:55,460 --> 00:05:00,790
But I think if you give me, um, one chance, I can change your mind.

88
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,420
Okay.

89
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,420
What?

90
00:05:03,590 --> 00:05:06,760
Okay. I'll give you one chance to change my mind.

91
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:09,050
You've got one minute.

92
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,970
Daddy.

93
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,970
Fine.

94
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:14,470
Two minutes. Go.

95
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,690
A minute and 50 seconds.

96
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,070
Okay, um...

97
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:26,400
I want you to know, I have never done anything like this before.

98
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:29,700
I mean, I've been in, um, relationships in general.

99
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:33,040
But I've never done it with a student. I mean, not...

100
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:37,620
Not "it." We haven't done "it."

101
00:05:37,790 --> 00:05:41,790
Uh... We, I mean... I mean, we've done stuff...

102
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:47,630
Okay. Okay. A joke. A joke. Lighten the mood.

103
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,680
Um, two guys go into a bar. One of them is Irish.

104
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:54,640
I'm Irish.

105
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:54,640
And the Irish guy wins the joke.

106
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,640
Ross?

107
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,640
Ross!

108
00:05:57,810 --> 00:06:01,980
How crazy that we would run into you.

109
00:05:57,810 --> 00:06:01,980
Oh, my God! Thank you.

110
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:06,190
Mr. Stevens, I'd like you to meet my friends.

111
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:08,280
This is Phoebe, Monica, and Chandler.

112
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:12,740
So you're Elizabeth's father, huh? I can see now where she gets her...

113
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:15,080
rugged handsomeness.

114
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,710
Is there a Mrs. Stevens?

115
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,880
There's a Mr. Bing!

116
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:28,720
No, unfortunately, Lizzie's mom passed away shortly after she was born.

117
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:31,840
I raised her by myself.

118
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:31,840
Oh...

119
00:06:32,010 --> 00:06:34,140
I get that a lot.

120
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:38,020
Okay, um, why don't we all take a seat, you know? Heh.

121
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:41,730
And, uh, I'll get us all some, uh, coffees.

122
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:44,560
Yeah, why don't you... Ahem. Uh...

123
00:06:44,730 --> 00:06:47,230
And you guys can talk about whatever you want.

124
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:50,400
Whatever pops into your head.

125
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:54,830
It is so strange seeing Ross here, this time of day...

126
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:57,450
because usually he's at the children's hospital.

127
00:06:57,620 --> 00:07:01,080
Yeah. But not looking for dates.

128
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:07,670
So, um, Monica is Ross' sister.

129
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:09,460
He's a great brother!

130
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:11,510
I had a sister.

131
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:11,510
Oh.

132
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,390
She passed away.

133
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,390
Oh...

134
00:07:13,550 --> 00:07:15,640
You don't have to do that every time.

135
00:07:16,390 --> 00:07:20,520
But, uh, Ross is a great guy. I was roommates with him in college.

136
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:23,100
Funny story, heh, ha, ha...

137
00:07:23,270 --> 00:07:26,310
Your roommate in college died, didn't he?

138
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,650
A part of him did, yes.

139
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:33,280
Okay! Here we are, Paul, Elizabeth.

140
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:36,070
I hope you guys were finding something to talk about.

141
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,120
Yes. We were just...

142
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:38,120
Sorry I'm late.

143
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:42,160
But I am ready, ready to talk you up. Heh.

144
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,920
When does Liz's father get here?

145
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,920
I'm already here.

146
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:48,670
Oh, Ross is so great.

147
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:57,140
Honey, you got the kind with the little girl. You said we'd get the kind with the baby.

148
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,640
You said the baby creeps you out.

149
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,640
The little girl creeps me out.

150
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:03,230
You said the baby.

151
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:03,230
Why would the baby creep me out?

152
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:06,150
Why would the little girl creep you out?

153
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:08,690
I'm sorry. Can you please talk a little slower.

154
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:11,190
This is for your book?

155
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:11,190
It's about relationships.

156
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:13,990
You know, the traps, the pitfalls, what not to do.

157
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,990
Keep going. This stuff's great.

158
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,990
What?

159
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,700
Excuse me.

160
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:22,660
And how none of it matters when the people really love each other.

161
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:28,960
And how people will believe anything you tell them as long as it's a compliment.

162
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:37,890
Oh, hi! Hi.

163
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:37,890
Hi. Hi.

164
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:41,430
I left my keys here somewhere.

165
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:41,430
Oh, well, let's look for them.

166
00:08:41,810 --> 00:08:43,890
Under here... Oh, hey!

167
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:46,060
Hey! Are these them?

168
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,520
No.

169
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,320
All right.

170
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,320
Oh.

171
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,030
Here they are.

172
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,030
Good.

173
00:08:57,030 --> 00:08:58,870
Mr. Paul?

174
00:08:57,030 --> 00:08:58,870
Just call me Paul.

175
00:08:59,030 --> 00:09:02,080
Paul. Um, I just wanted you to know that...

176
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,660
you know, Ross really is a great guy.

177
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:08,420
Maybe you could date him then. It would save me the trouble of killing him.

178
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:14,630
Are you okay?

179
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,630
You just don't look old enough to have a 20-year-old daughter.

180
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,590
Well, we were very young when we had her.

181
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:24,390
Ah. We?

182
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:24,390
Yeah, it usually takes two people to...

183
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:26,940
Oh, no! Yes! Of course. I know that.

184
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:31,690
What I meant was are you still "we" or are you just you?

185
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:33,980
I'm just me. Yeah.

186
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:36,820
My wife died shortly after Lizzie was born.

187
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:38,150
Oh.

188
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:42,120
So you raised her all on your own?

189
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:42,120
Yes, I did.

190
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,580
Oh...

191
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:49,080
Hey.

192
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:49,080
Hey.

193
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:51,000
How was your first day?

194
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:51,000
Great.

195
00:09:51,170 --> 00:09:53,630
Except I got a little attitude from the robot.

196
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:57,130
Damn those robots. They're supposed to be our faithful servants!

197
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,720
It wasn't the robot, it was the guy who controls him.

198
00:10:00,890 --> 00:10:04,220
He doesn't like me. He had C.H.E.E.S.E. Knock over the sandwich table...

199
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:06,770
right when I was reaching for one. Ugh.

200
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:08,600
Why don't you get him fired?

201
00:10:08,770 --> 00:10:12,440
I may have to. I hate to do it. But I'm the star, you know?

202
00:10:12,610 --> 00:10:15,900
There's a limit to how many sandwiches I can eat off the floor.

203
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:20,110
Excuse me.

204
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,570
Joey Tribbiani.

205
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:26,450
Joe! I'm glad I found you! I got an audition for you.

206
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:29,620
Wow.

207
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:29,620
The thing is, it's kind of on the q.t.

208
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:33,710
The actor who has the part doesn't know he might be fired.

209
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,840
It's the lead in a series.

210
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,760
Mac and C.H.E.E.S.E.

211
00:10:39,590 --> 00:10:41,340
I'm the lead in Mac and C.H.E.E.S.E.

212
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:43,760
Uh-oh.

213
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:48,220
Joey?

214
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:51,270
Hi, Ross.

215
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:57,780
I was just getting him to like you.

216
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,240
Joey?

217
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,620
Joey!

218
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,620
Hey, Ross.

219
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:11,620
Ross, Joey is not here.

220
00:11:11,790 --> 00:11:14,040
Okay, I'll just wait for him in here!

221
00:11:14,210 --> 00:11:16,800
Ross, it's okay. You can come out.

222
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:19,420
Yeah, Ross. It's okay. It's me...

223
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:21,420
Mr. Stevens.

224
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:26,720
Oh, I didn't... Oh, my gosh. I didn't even see you.

225
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:29,930
Sure you did. You came in, got all awkward and ran to the bedroom.

226
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,060
You were shouting, "Joey, Joey!"

227
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:36,110
Bye, Rachel.

228
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:36,110
Bye.

229
00:11:36,270 --> 00:11:37,940
I'll call you later.

230
00:11:36,270 --> 00:11:37,940
Okay. See you!

231
00:11:38,110 --> 00:11:40,740
Bye, Ross.

232
00:11:38,110 --> 00:11:40,740
Ah, hoo. Ha, ha.

233
00:11:42,150 --> 00:11:45,780
What? What the...? How did...? What?

234
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:51,120
You know, he lost his keys. So he was looking for them.

235
00:11:51,290 --> 00:11:52,710
In your mouth?

236
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:56,500
No.

237
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:58,750
Downstairs. And we got to talking...

238
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:03,220
for two hours. I really liked him. I invited him for a cup of coffee.

239
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:06,300
You were at the coffee house!

240
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,390
Ross, what's the big deal? So I kissed the guy.

241
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:14,810
He's my girlfriend's father. Okay? It's weird!

242
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:18,110
You dated my sister.

243
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:18,110
That was different!

244
00:12:18,270 --> 00:12:22,400
What? Why?

245
00:12:18,270 --> 00:12:22,400
This is weird for me!

246
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:26,280
Ross, look. This is good for you, okay?

247
00:12:26,450 --> 00:12:29,530
Let's face it. So far the guy's not loving you.

248
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:32,950
But I can turn that around. I've got the inside track.

249
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:37,000
We could all go out to dinner. And I could talk you up.

250
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:41,500
Plus the guy is a very, very successful lawyer.

251
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,880
How is that important?

252
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,880
Oh, it's important.

253
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,640
There's a million guys out there who can play Mac...

254
00:12:50,810 --> 00:12:52,180
and there's only one robot.

255
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:55,850
And this one guy who controls it. I didn't know he could get me fired.

256
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:58,020
What am I gonna do?

257
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:58,020
Well, Joey.

258
00:12:58,190 --> 00:13:00,480
You're a pretty charming guy.

259
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:02,860
Thanks. But I have a problem to deal with.

260
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:06,280
No, sweetie. You've got to win over the guy who controls C.H.E.E.S.E.

261
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:10,370
Go back there and kiss some serious robot ass!

262
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,370
That's not a bad idea!

263
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:18,080
If I have to turn on the charm tomorrow, I'm not wasting any of it on you guys.

264
00:13:18,250 --> 00:13:21,590
Oh, actually I got a little bit saved for you, Pheebs.

265
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:27,630
So do you think, uh, Joey is more charming than me?

266
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,390
Yeah. That's why I'm sleeping with him on the side.

267
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:32,680
Yeah, you wish.

268
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:39,350
"You wish."

269
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:39,350
Phoebe, stop writing about us.

270
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:42,980
I'm not writing about you. I'm writing about other people.

271
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:46,900
Who?

272
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:46,900
Marsha and Chester.

273
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:52,120
Okay, fine. Fine. Then you know what? I will just write about Phyllis.

274
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,330
Hmm.

275
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,330
Huh.

276
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:57,000
"Phyllis is sitting in the chair."

277
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:57,000
I see what you're doing.

278
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,960
"Phyllis sees what I'm doing."

279
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:59,960
Oh, ho.

280
00:14:01,210 --> 00:14:05,420
Ooh, I have tasted my own medicine and it is bitter.

281
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,930
Morning! Hey!

282
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:15,430
How's my favorite genius and his robot buddy?

283
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:19,310
Don't touch him!

284
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:19,310
Okay. All right. Um...

285
00:14:19,850 --> 00:14:24,270
Wayne, level with me. I keep hearing all these rumors that I might get fired.

286
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:27,650
They even have actors coming in to read for my part.

287
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:30,320
Come on, man. You gotta give me a second chance.

288
00:14:30,490 --> 00:14:33,070
I love this little guy... Aah.

289
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:37,790
Okay. That's why you didn't want me to touch him, right? There you go.

290
00:14:39,790 --> 00:14:42,830
Stupid! I can't believe this! God.

291
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:47,010
Hey, how are you doing?

292
00:14:51,890 --> 00:14:55,390
So it seemed that my prom date had stood me up.

293
00:14:55,560 --> 00:15:00,140
So Ross selflessly offered to take me.

294
00:15:00,310 --> 00:15:02,520
What a nice story.

295
00:15:00,310 --> 00:15:02,520
Heh.

296
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:04,230
So Ross was in college...

297
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:07,860
and decided to jump at the chance to take a young girl to her prom.

298
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:14,780
Wow. I definitely did not see that one backfiring.

299
00:15:14,950 --> 00:15:18,450
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

300
00:15:14,950 --> 00:15:18,450
Yeah. Take your time.

301
00:15:20,790 --> 00:15:25,000
Just so you know, I was a freshman and she was a senior. So it wasn't as bad as...

302
00:15:25,170 --> 00:15:29,260
Ross, look. I know I've been giving you a lot of jabs.

303
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:33,050
It's partly because I'm very protective of Lizzie...

304
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:36,970
and partly because they just keep coming to me.

305
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:43,100
I have to admit that after all the wonderful things Lizzie has told me...

306
00:15:43,270 --> 00:15:48,980
and the many, many, many stories that Rachel has told me...

307
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:51,280
that, well...

308
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,110
you're not...

309
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:56,700
all bad.

310
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:00,450
"Not all bad."

311
00:16:00,620 --> 00:16:04,500
I'm sorry I was so harsh. But you have to understand.

312
00:16:04,670 --> 00:16:08,210
I still look at Lizzie like she's a 12-year-old girl.

313
00:16:08,380 --> 00:16:12,340
You know, I know what you mean. I do that, too.

314
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:18,890
I beg your pardon?

315
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:18,890
No! I don't see her as a 12-year-old girl.

316
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:23,140
I mean, I have a son who's, um, 6, and I still think of him as a baby.

317
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:25,810
You have a son?

318
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:25,810
Yeah. My ex-wife and I...

319
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:28,770
uh, share custody of Ben. And, uh...

320
00:16:28,940 --> 00:16:31,610
Just so you know, Carol and I are on excellent terms...

321
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:33,570
as I'm sure you are with your wife.

322
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:35,700
Oh! I'm sorry.

323
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:38,910
It's unbelievable!

324
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:42,000
Don't worry. I just didn't realize you were married.

325
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,790
Oh, we were. But that was just a...

326
00:16:48,170 --> 00:16:51,750
I mean, that was just a big drunken mistake.

327
00:16:54,550 --> 00:16:56,050
You're back.

328
00:16:58,180 --> 00:17:00,350
You two were married?

329
00:17:00,510 --> 00:17:03,470
Oh, whoops. I'm sorry. You were talking about Emily.

330
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:09,440
We said we would meet at the coffee house at 6:00.

331
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:12,530
We said 7:00.

332
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:12,530
We said 6:00!

333
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:14,690
The only way that I said 6:00...

334
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:19,950
would be if I said the sentence, "Let's meet at 7:00, not at 6:00."

335
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:23,160
If I had said 7:00, I would have said something like:

336
00:17:23,330 --> 00:17:27,420
"Wow, my boyfriend is such a wiseass. 7:00!"

337
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,710
Hi!

338
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,710
Oh, my good God!

339
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:33,170
I know what time you said.

340
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:33,170
What?

341
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:36,720
Well, actually I know what time Chester and Marsha said.

342
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,760
What time?

343
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,760
Quite an interesting turn of events.

344
00:17:40,930 --> 00:17:44,770
Suddenly it's my book to the rescue, huh? Let's see.

345
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:47,640
Ooh. Very interesting.

346
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:50,440
Yeah, well this certainly clears things up.

347
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:53,110
What does it say?

348
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:53,110
I will tell you...

349
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,440
as soon as you thank me for writing my book.

350
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:00,620
Thank you for writing your book. It's a great book...

351
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:04,740
and you are the queen of everything.

352
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:07,870
Thanks. So are you.

353
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:16,130
I told you I should not wear this color.

354
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:25,010
"Monica... Marsha and Chester are planning on seeing a movie Sunday night.

355
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:27,350
"Marsha thinks they're supposed to meet at 6:00.

356
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,440
Chester thinks it's at 7:00."

357
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:33,610
You knew we would miss the movie?

358
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:33,610
That's right.

359
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:37,440
Instead of telling us, you decided to write it in your stupid book?

360
00:18:38,110 --> 00:18:40,860
"Marsha and Chester are mad at Phyllis."

361
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,000
I can't believe I'm gonna lose this job.

362
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,790
I'm so sorry, man. Is there anything I can do?

363
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:55,380
Yeah. Help me get this mini-fridge past the security guard.

364
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:03,720
Hey, Joey, I want to talk to you.

365
00:19:03,890 --> 00:19:08,310
Yeah? I don't want to talk to you, Wayne. I hate you. You ruined my life.

366
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:11,100
Oh, Chandler, Wayne. Wayne, Chandler.

367
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:11,100
Hi. How are you?

368
00:19:11,770 --> 00:19:15,400
Joey, I'll get you your job back if you help me out.

369
00:19:15,570 --> 00:19:17,610
Why should I help you out?

370
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:21,700
The reason he just said.

371
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:21,700
What do you need?

372
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:26,330
I saw you on stage talking to that beautiful woman.

373
00:19:26,490 --> 00:19:30,120
You know, Sarah. I wish I could talk to her.

374
00:19:30,290 --> 00:19:32,670
Are you in love with her?

375
00:19:30,290 --> 00:19:32,670
Yeah.

376
00:19:32,830 --> 00:19:35,590
Her. All of them. Anyone.

377
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:38,050
Yeah. I've been there, my friend.

378
00:19:38,670 --> 00:19:41,260
Listen, I guarantee you keep your job...

379
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:44,260
if you can teach me how to talk to women like you do.

380
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:49,680
Oh, Wayne, it's not something you can teach. It's something you're born with...

381
00:19:49,850 --> 00:19:52,600
You can teach it. I can show you right now.

382
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:55,730
I mean, if you think about it...

383
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:59,110
Ross did learn something from each marriage.

384
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:02,200
How to make the next one even shorter?

385
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:02,200
Oh.

386
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,990
Wait a minute. That's not fair.

387
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:07,330
He was married to me a hell of a lot longer than he was to Emily.

388
00:20:07,490 --> 00:20:09,660
He just didn't tell me.

389
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:15,250
Maybe I have to pee again.

390
00:20:20,340 --> 00:20:22,260
Well, this is fun.

391
00:20:22,970 --> 00:20:24,760
So Ross...

392
00:20:24,930 --> 00:20:26,800
did you kill any of these wives?

393
00:20:27,010 --> 00:20:28,390
You know what? I...

394
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:33,100
I have had enough of this. I care a great deal about your daughter.

395
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:35,730
And I have treated her with nothing but respect.

396
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:38,100
So if you've got a problem with me...

397
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:39,400
Are you yelling at me?

398
00:20:39,570 --> 00:20:41,530
God, no.

399
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:46,490
You know what, Daddy? If you don't like Ross, that's fine.

400
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:49,950
It doesn't matter to me. I'm gonna go out with him anyway.

401
00:20:50,450 --> 00:20:52,040
Really?

402
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,410
Well, if it doesn't matter to her...

403
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:57,630
it doesn't matter to me. Still not yelling.

404
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:03,300
Well, what can I say?

405
00:21:06,550 --> 00:21:08,260
This doesn't make me like you better.

406
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:11,760
That's okay. I'm not so crazy about myself right now either.

407
00:21:11,930 --> 00:21:14,520
Then we agree?

408
00:21:11,930 --> 00:21:14,520
Yeah, I guess so.

409
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,480
Neither of us like Ross.

410
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,480
I like Ross.

411
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:19,360
Oh, heh, kids!

412
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:24,940
Wait. I just thought of another story about how nice Ross is.

413
00:21:25,110 --> 00:21:27,740
That's okay, Rach. We're not liking Ross right now.

414
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:30,530
Oh! Well, I got a lot of those, too.

415
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:30,530
Uh...

416
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:37,330
Well, it turns out you were right, C.H.E.E.S.E.

417
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:40,920
That shipment never made it to Omaha?

418
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:40,920
You got it.

419
00:21:41,090 --> 00:21:44,880
And the rabbi's beard? 100 percent horse hair.

420
00:21:45,050 --> 00:21:46,670
Nice catch, C.H.E.E.S.E.

421
00:21:51,970 --> 00:21:53,970
It's your line, C.H.E.E.S.E.

422
00:21:56,730 --> 00:21:58,730
Wayne! Wayne!

